 "result": "Start with these, in order:\n\n1. **`src/tessel/app.py:364`**: `static_cache_seconds(filename)` sets the `max_age` for static files. Override it to change the lifetime. The static view that calls it is around line 407.\n2. **`src/tessel/bundles.py:56` and `:99`**: the same hook and static view for bundles, which may have their own override.\n3. **`src/tessel/helpers.py:405-406`, `:463-474`**: `send_file` falls back to `app.static_cache_seconds` when `max_age` is not given. This is where the `Cache-Control` header and conditional/ETag handling come from.\n\nThe usual cause is a long or unset max-age combined with unversioned filenames like `style.css`. Browsers keep the cached copy until it expires and never revalidate. The fix is to shorten the max-age or to cache-bust the URLs, for example with `?v=<hash>` or hashed filenames.\n\nIf a reverse proxy or CDN such as nginx serves `/static` directly, its own cache headers bypass all of this. I didn't check for that config in this repo.",
